umption: The quote list can be curated locally in `script.js`.\n- Assumption: The app should work by opening `index.html` directly.\n- Local validation expected: test -f index.html; test -f styles.css; test -f script.js; test -f README.md; test -f .head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md; node --check script.js; test -f index.html && test -f styles.css && test -f script.js && test -f README.md\n## Proposed Product Direction\nA single-page static quote board with a header, quote cards, favorite buttons, and a favorites/all toggle. JavaScript manages rendering, favorite state, and `localStorage` persistence. CSS provides a polished responsive layout without external dependencies.\n## Codex Orchestration\n- One local Codex CLI session owns the repo.\n- Codex decides how many internal subagents are useful; for non-trivial work it should prefer visible named responsibility lanes when that is truthful.\n- Subagents are logical Codex responsibilities, not Docker, VM, GKE, or cloud workers.\n- The user can revise subagent use before approval; approval permits Codex to choose the actual internal count and names.\n- If Codex later determines a materially different subagent strategy is needed, it must stop and ask before changing scope, cost, risk, or timeline.\n- The browser flowchart updates rapidly from a parallel Codex flowchart process and shows only the subagents Codex actually reports.\n## Subagent Check-In\n- Advisor recommendation: single-lane Codex run is acceptable.\n- Reason: The Codex planner produced a narrow responsibility split, so a direct implementation lane looks sufficient.\n- User check-in: The plan looks narrow enough for a direct Codex lane. Approval keeps Codex free to ask before changing to a materially different subagent strategy.\n- Likely responsibility areas: Build static app\n- Advisor source: planner_context\n## Continuous Improvement Loop\n- Codex should look for bugs, UX gaps, performance issues, maintainability problems, missing tests, and feature opportunities while implementing.\n- Codex may implement improvements that fit the approved plan or are required for correctness, validation, safety, or a trustworthy MVP.\n- Codex must record deferred ideas in `.head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md` instead of silently expanding scope.\n- Improvements that materially change scope, architecture, data, cost, risk, or timeline require user approval before implementation.\n## Codex Runtime\n- Model: gpt-5.5\n- Coding reasoning: low\n- Planning/model helper reasoning: gpt-5.5 / low\n- Access: full local access\n- Shell environment: inherited from the local supervisor process\n- Account/config/plugins: same local Codex account and CODEX_HOME configuration used by this machine\n## Proposed Internal Responsibilities\n1. Build static app - Create a new static browser-only Codexa project named `codexa-private-r4-01-quote-board-1780177220` with `index.html`, `styles.css`, `script.js`, `README.md`, local validation, saved favorite quotes via browser storage, and concise progress updates. Implementation must wait for user approval.. Validation: test -f index.html, test -f styles.css, test -f script.js, test -f README.md, test -f .head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md, node --check script.js, test -f index.html && test -f styles.css && test -f script.js && test -f README.md.\n## Assumptions\n- Favorites will be persisted with `localStorage`.\n- The app will be static and browser-only with no build step or package installation.\n- The quote list can be curated locally in `script.js`.\n- The app should work by opening `index.html` directly.\n## Open Questions\n- None recorded yet.\n## Validation Plan\n- test -f index.html\n- test -f styles.css\n- test -f script.js\n- test -f README.md\n- test -f .head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md\n- node --check script.js\n- test -f index.html && test -f styles.css && test -f script.js && test -f README.md\n## Completion Bar\n- Files exist in this repo.\n- Validation commands pass or failures are reported honestly.\n